AUTHORITY -- WHAT THE PRODUCT IS SUPPOSED TO DO, READ BEFORE GRADING
=================================================================================
Per memory `review-feature-docs-before-testing`.  This case turns entirely on the authority,
so all of it is quoted rather than summarised.  Both documents are saved in work/.

(1) SOFTWARE TPS -- "X960 platform support TPS"
    https://wiki.atlnz.lc/awpwiki/index.php/X960_platform_support_TPS  (fetched 2026-10-20)
    Case-title numbers map to TPS rows with a constant -2 offset, verified against group A
    (case "(274) Local RADIUS Server" <-> TPS row 272).  Case (273) is therefore TPS row 271:

        TPS row 271 | Management | Show warning message when user continue to use default PW
                    | Priority 1 | Supported: YES

    The TPS wording is almost the case title verbatim.  => the feature is DECLARED SUPPORTED
    on the x960.  An absence is a FINDING, not a platform limit.

(2) THE FEATURE'S OWN TFS -- "Warning when using default password TFS", project 2616,
    revision 0.3, approved by the Product Owner, Global PM, Security Team, Factory and Team
    Lead in Oct 2021; raised by MRS-1071.
    https://wiki.atlnz.lc/awpwiki/index.php/Warning_when_using_default_password_TFS
    (saved verbatim in work/authority-TFS-2616-warning-when-using-default-password.wiki)

    Key Concepts, verbatim:
      "When a user logs in to the device using the default login account 'manager', the device
       will check if the default account's password is the same as the factory default, if it
       is the same, the system will warn the user that the default password ('friend') for the
       default login account should be changed."

    Spec 2616.1, verbatim:
      "The system will check at every login using the default account 'manager' if the factory
       default password 'friend' is set, if it is, the system will warn the user that the
       default password should be changed."

    and the worked example, verbatim:

       awplus login: manager
       Password:
       AlliedWare Plus (TM) 0.0.0 09/26/21 21:23:17
       % Default password needs to be changed.
       awplus>

    Other sections of that TFS, which between them remove every alternative explanation:
      Feature functionality that will NOT be implemented : None
      Command Line Interface specifications / New Commands / Configuration Commands : None
      Logging specifications : None
      Licensing : part of the standard feature set, no licensing requirements
      Initial Release Targets : "This feature will be released on all platforms in 5.5.1-2"
      Excluded Targets : None

    => the expected string is exactly `% Default password needs to be changed.`, printed
    after the version banner and immediately before the first prompt, at EVERY login as
    `manager` while the password is `friend`; it needs NO configuration, NO licence, and is
    targeted at ALL platforms from 5.5.1-2.  The DUT runs sin_x96056-20261012-24, far beyond
    5.5.1-2.  Because the TFS specifies no log line and no show command, the login byte
    stream is the ONLY place this can be graded -- which is why this group needed a network
    login driver (tools/netlogin.py).

(3) THE RELATED, OLDER FEATURE -- "Default Password Change TFS" (ER361, FDPC = Forced Default
    Password Change), and the CURRENT engineering page "Forced Default Password Change"
    https://wiki.atlnz.lc/awpwiki/index.php/Forced_Default_Password_Change
    (saved verbatim in work/authority-wiki-Forced-Default-Password-Change.wiki)

    These were found by searching the wiki for the exact string in the 2616 example, and they
    matter because they share that string and they explain the measured result.

    ER361.1.02, verbatim:
      "If the kernel argument or boot environment variable 'def_pwd_chg' is set with value of
       "1", the system will check if the default account 'manager' is set with the facory
       default password 'friend', if it is, the system will display warnings "% Default
       password needs to be changed.". Also a log of WARNING severity will be generated,
       "Default password for user 'manager' needs to be changed.""

    FDPC originates from a South Korean market requirement, is gated on a U-Boot environment
    variable set by the factory or the supply chain, and FORCES a password change.  2616 is
    the later, ungated, warn-only feature, and it is 2616 that the TPS row and this case name.

    *** The current engineering page's "Default Password Detection" section, VERBATIM -- this
    is the single most important sentence in this case: ***

      "Currently, we only check that the password has been encrypted with an MD5 hash, as the
       default-generated config contains this but a user-generated config will not.
       This means that the most likely way to see the password warning is if the user has
       copied the value from the factory-generated config into a new config."

    The same page also states a SECOND, independently testable consequence, which this case
    uses as corroboration (STEP 5):

      "The HTTP server disallows most APIs when the default password still needs to be changed
       (i.e. when the device is in the "Factory-default password" state defined above). During
       this mode, only the APIs which are required for the initial login/password change flow
       are accessible. ... Other APIs will return some form of HTTP 403 Forbidden response with
       the error message `API access requires admin password to be configured` ... RestCONF
       returns ... "error-tag": "access-denied", "error-message": "API access requires admin
       password to be configured"."

