---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 4 -- NEGATIVE CONTROL: an account whose password is NOT the factory default
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Designed expectation: `ckalt`, password `testing123`, must NOT be warned -- 2616.1 scopes the
check to "the default account 'manager'".  This control shows the login path is otherwise
identical, so a difference would have been visible had there been one.

    tools/tb tool tb277 ckmgmt netlogin --proto telnet --host 10.38.22.34 --user ckalt
        --password testing123 --login-timeout 20

    --- bytes after the password was sent (THE LOGIN BANNER) ---

    No entry for terminal type "network";
    using vt100 terminal settings.
    AlliedWare Plus (TM) 0.0.0 10/12/26 06:38:00

    awplus>
    LOGIN RESULT: USER  proto=telnet  user=ckalt  seconds=0.2

Byte-for-byte the same shape as `manager`'s telnet login, minus one line: there is NO
`Last login:` for `ckalt`, because it had never logged in before and the line comes from the
Linux lastlog of a local account (platforms/x960.md §7E.2).  No warning, as expected.
SSH was not used for this control: `ssh server allow-users manager` restricts SSH to the
`manager` account, and widening it would have been a configuration change with no extra
discrimination to buy.  Stated rather than silently skipped.
STEP 4 VERDICT: PASS -- the control behaves as the TFS says it should.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 5 -- ACCESS PATH 4: HTTP.  There is no web login to observe, and the HTTP
          subsystem independently reports that the DUT is NOT in the default-password state
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Designed expectation, part one: if a Web GUI is installed, log in through it and look for the
warning.  Part two, from authority (3): if the device considered itself to be in the
"Factory-default password" state it would be in LOGIN-ONLY MODE and its APIs would answer
403 Forbidden with `API access requires admin password to be configured`.  That is a test of
the SAME internal check through a COMPLETELY DIFFERENT subsystem -- not IMISH, but the HTTP
server -- and it needs no login at all.

5a. Is there a GUI?  `show http` -> `Web GUI Information / GUI file in use : -`.
    NO GUI file is installed.  Installing one needs `activate flash:/Load-gui9.sh`, a
    temporary IP and a route to 10.32.18.135 (memory `awplus-gui-load-script`) -- a bench
    change, not made unattended.

5b. What does the web server actually answer?  (work/v-http-probe2.log)

    GET http://10.38.22.34/           -> 301 to https, then HTTP 404 Not Found, nginx, 146 B
    GET https://10.38.22.34/          -> HTTP 404 Not Found, nginx, 146 B
    GET https://10.38.22.34/login     -> HTTP 404 Not Found  (with manager/friend basic auth)
    POST https://10.38.22.34/ username=manager&password=friend -> HTTP 404 Not Found

    The server is alive (TLS up, `Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'`,
    `X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN`, `Server: nginx`) and has nothing to serve, consistent with
    `GUI file in use : -`.  The DUT's own log says the same thing from the inside:
        2026 Oct 19 22:59:42 daemon.err awplus nginx[2192]: open()
        "/usr/html/public/login.html" failed (2: No such file or directory), client:
        10.38.22.33, ... request: "GET /public/login.html HTTP/1.1"
    (that `daemon.err` is MY probe's doing, and is not a fault.)
    => THERE IS NO HTTP LOGIN TO OBSERVE ON THIS DUT.  That limb is NOT MEASURABLE, and the
    reason is measured rather than assumed.

5c. *** The login-only-mode test, which IS measurable and is the key corroboration ***
    (work/v-http-api.log)

    GET https://10.38.22.34/api            (manager/friend) -> HTTP 404, Content-Length 0
    GET https://10.38.22.34/api/v1/system  (manager/friend) -> HTTP 501
        {"code":"ANT_CODE_UNIMPLEMENTED","message":"Unknown url and verb combination"}
    GET https://10.38.22.34/restconf/data  (manager/friend) -> *** HTTP 200 OK ***
        Content-Type: application/yang-data+json, Content-Length: 11848
        {"ietf-yang-library:yang-library": {"module-set": [{"name": "common", "module":
         [{"name": "AT-POWER-ETHERNET-MIB-DEVIATION", ...

    RestCONF served a full 11848-byte normal response.  Per authority (3), had the device
    considered itself to be in the "Factory-default password" state, that request would have
    returned 403 with `"error-tag": "access-denied", "error-message": "API access requires
    admin password to be configured"`.  It did not.

    *** So the DUT's HTTP subsystem agrees with its CLI: the device does NOT believe its
    manager password is the factory default -- although the password literally IS `friend`. ***
    Two independent subsystems, one answer.
STEP 5 VERDICT: HTTP login NOT MEASURABLE (no GUI); login-only-mode corroboration PASS and
decisive.

